# Thornbeast — a bramble-hulk for the FPS roster, authored from a 2D concept
# plate (docs/dev-notes/refs/thornbeast-reference.png, a Meshy AI generation
# the owner supplied). The plate is INSPIRATION and DIRECTION, not a fit
# target — the owner explicitly did not provide a mesh for exactly the reason
# the gargoyle notes record: measuring ate the session. Every number below is
# therefore EYEBALLED off the plate and tuned by eye against turntable frames;
# the `# plate:` comments say what each number is matching.
#
# THE READ, in silhouette order: a rust-barked hulk with a MASSIVE shoulder
# yoke riding over a small sunken head, arms so long the clawed fingertips
# reach the knees, rows of pale thorns raking back along the outer forearms,
# quill fans bursting from the shoulders and upper back, thin legs ending in
# big two-claw talon feet. No tail, no wings, no big ears — the gargoyle owns
# all three; this one is thorns. The hide is rust-brown bark blotched with
# olive-green; thorns and claws are pale bone; the eyes are two tiny embers
# sunk under a heavy monobrow shelf.
#
# FACE: no mesh exists to bake, so the face is authored prims in the
# goblin/gargoyle idiom (multiple blended orbs + shaped prims, face block
# shrunk to a nub) plus a HAND-AUTHORED maw decal at MULTIPLY — the gargoyle's
# third-road precedent (painted prims read as a visor; the generated sheet
# reads as the zombie; geometric teeth read as a walrus goatee).
model thornbeast
  height 2.1
  # Checked, not decorative: the plate's legs bend like a man's (knee forward,
  # ankle back under the body) — unlike the gargoyle's bird fold, which is the
  # deliberate point of difference. See blob-checks.ts.
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # Hip line at 1.10 (root 0.98 + len 0.12; children attach at the TAIL).
  # 0.52 of height — a tall gangly upright hulk, NOT the gargoyle's crouched
  # 0.28: the plate's legs are long and the mass rides high on the yoke.
  root pelvis at 0.98 len=0.12

  # Hunched chain: the plate's chest sits forward over the hips and the head
  # sinks INTO the yoke, so the pitches lean the spine ~26 deg total while the
  # SHORT forward-thrust neck drops the skull between the shoulders — the jaw
  # mass hangs BELOW the shoulder tops (the sunken read the plate has and the
  # gargoyle comment calls "jaw line below the shoulder tops"). Neck+skull
  # pitch 22+10, NOT steeper: at 30+22 the face plane tipped so far under the
  # slab's brim that it lived in its own shadow and vanished from every
  # front camera. Crown of the head lands ~1.9; the crown thorns carry the
  # figure to the declared 2.1.
  bone spine parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=14 len=0.27
  bone chest parent=spine dir=up pitch=12 len=0.25
  bone neck  parent=chest dir=up pitch=22 len=0.11
  bone skull parent=neck  dir=up pitch=10 len=0.15

  mirror
    # Shoulder socket at x ~0.20, just proud of the chest's ~0.23 half-width
    # (the yoke blob below owns the width; the goblin lesson is shoulder reach
    # is a function of chest width).
    bone clavicle parent=chest  dir=side len=0.13 side=0.07
    # The absurd reach: upper 0.42 + fore 0.40 + hand 0.15 puts the wrist at
    # y ~0.87 and the fingertips at knee level (~0.62) — the plate's hands
    # hang past mid-thigh, in FRONT of the body (z ~0.2, clear of the thighs).
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=10 pitch=8  len=0.42
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=4  pitch=6  len=0.40
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down pitch=14 len=0.15
    # Humanoid leg: thigh pitch +4, shin pitch -6 so the knee falls FORWARD of
    # the hip->ankle chord (+42 mm, passes checkStance as humanoid); the ankle
    # swings back under the body. Big talon foot: a long slanted segment to a
    # toe joint at the ground (foot pitch 42).
    bone thigh parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=4  tilt=8 side=0.10 len=0.50
    bone shin  parent=thigh  dir=down pitch=-6            len=0.46
    bone foot  parent=shin   dir=down pitch=42            len=0.18
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — four masses: haunch, belly, chest, and the YOKE. The yoke is the
  # character: a shoulder shelf 0.61 wide, WIDER than the chest and rising
  # above the head's jaw — the plate's shoulders are its whole silhouette.
  # The bark read comes from the palette's mottle.
  # ============================================================
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.45 r=0.150 wide=1.55 tall=1.00 deep=1.20 blend=0.020
  blob torso on spine  at=0.40 r=0.145 wide=1.40 tall=1.05 deep=1.55 blend=0.020
  blob torso on chest  at=0.40 r=0.150 wide=1.70 tall=1.25 deep=1.40 blend=0.020
  # The yoke: rides the neck bone so it caps the chest from above and swallows
  # the jaw (the head sinks in). semi-x 0.31 — the widest prim on the body.
  blob torso on neck   at=0.25 r=0.105 wide=2.95 tall=0.80 deep=1.05 blend=0.014

  # Neck: thick column, mostly swallowed by the yoke (the head sits IN it).
  bar head on neck from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.068 deep=0.90 blend=0.008

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS — the reach. One mass per segment plus palm and three claw lines
  # per hand; the forearm bars carry thorn rows (below). Heavy deltoid caps
  # so the arms read as growing out of the yoke, not pinned to it.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on upperarm at=0.10 r=0.105 blend=0.012 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.15 to=0.95 r=0.082 r2=0.052 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.05 to=0.92 r=0.062 r2=0.040 blend=0.008 mirror
  blob arm on hand at=0.50 r=0.050 wide=1.10 tall=0.85 deep=1.30 blend=0.006 mirror
  # Fingers: three knuckle bars per hand. Under plain mirror each line's
  # offset.x reflects on the .r hand, so the splayed pair lands at +-0.028 on
  # BOTH hands and the centre line fills the middle — a three-claw spread
  # matching the plate's long spiky fingers. chamfer + small r2 = claw points.
  bar arm on hand from=0.80 to=1.35 r=0.022 r2=0.008 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.028,0.008,0.004) tip=(0.010,-0.062,0.052) mirror
  bar arm on hand from=0.80 to=1.35 r=0.020 r2=0.007 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.000,0.006,0.000) tip=(0.000,-0.070,0.046) mirror
  bar arm on hand from=0.80 to=1.35 r=0.022 r2=0.008 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(-0.028,0.008,-0.002) tip=(-0.010,-0.058,0.048) mirror
  # Knuckle thorn: one pale spike off the back of each hand.
  bar arm on hand from=0.30 to=0.55 r=0.013 r2=0.002 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.005,0.048,-0.012) tip=(0.004,0.045,-0.045) mirror color=c9b896

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — humanoid, thin under the massive top: fat thigh tapering hard,
  # slim shin, swollen ankle, one long slanted talon segment to a toe pad and
  # a splayed two-claw pair (the plate's feet show two big forward talons).
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.05 r=0.105 blend=0.012 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.10 to=0.95 r=0.095 r2=0.060 deep=1.05 blend=0.012 mirror
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.055 r2=0.042 blend=0.008 mirror
  blob leg on foot  at=0.02 r=0.060 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  leg on foot  from=0.10 to=0.90 r=0.055 r2=0.045 blend=0.010 mirror
  # Toe pad: the ground-contact fan under the talon segment's end.
  blob leg on foot at=1.00 offset=(0.030,-0.015,0.030) r=0.050 wide=1.40 tall=0.70 deep=1.40 blend=0.008 mirror
  # Talons: dark, chamfered to points, a splayed pair per foot (as with the
  # fingers, each line's offset.x reflects on the .r foot).
  bar leg on foot from=0.95 to=1.12 r=0.026 r2=0.005 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.028,-0.025,0.075) tip=(0.010,-0.028,0.050) mirror color=26201a
  bar leg on foot from=0.95 to=1.12 r=0.024 r2=0.005 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(-0.028,-0.025,0.070) tip=(-0.012,-0.026,0.046) mirror color=26201a

  # ============================================================
  # THORNS — the plate's signature. Pale bone (c9b896) so they read against
  # the rust hide at gameplay distance; every base is seated INSIDE its host
  # prim's flesh (the gargoyle wing-spur strandedOf lesson) and rakes BACK
  # like a bramble. Kept to 16 thorn prims total so the cluster budget and
  # the raymarch cost stay at the gargoyle's scale. First pass had thin
  # quills off the clavicles and they read as insect ANTENNAE framing the
  # head — round 2 moves the big pair onto the YOKE itself, thick, rising
  # up-out like the plate's shoulder burst.
  # ============================================================
  # Yoke burst: one BIG thick pair rising up-out-back off the yoke's top
  # slope, plus a smaller pair behind it (both = the pair; neck is a centre
  # bone, torso cluster — nothing severs). Bases are seated INSIDE the yoke
  # ellipsoid (centre ~(0,1.631,0.130), semi 0.31/0.084/0.11) — a first pass
  # launched them off the slope's AIR and strandedOf caught 33 mm of float.
  bar torso on neck from=0.30 to=0.90 r=0.030 r2=0.005 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.200,0.029,0.056) tip=(0.110,0.260,-0.090) both color=c9b896
  bar torso on neck from=0.20 to=0.70 r=0.022 r2=0.003 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.240,0.024,-0.034) tip=(0.090,0.180,-0.130) both color=c9b896
  # Forearm row, outer: rakes back-up off the outer edge (offset.x mirrors
  # outward on the .r arm); pokes well clear of the r~0.055 forearm flesh.
  bar arm on forearm from=0.30 to=0.55 r=0.018 r2=0.003 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.058,0.015,-0.020) tip=(0.022,0.055,-0.075) mirror color=c9b896
  # Forearm row, rear: sits on the back of the forearm, pointing back.
  bar arm on forearm from=0.55 to=0.78 r=0.016 r2=0.003 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(-0.008,0.010,-0.058) tip=(-0.005,0.055,-0.065) mirror color=c9b896
  # Back fan: two tall quills per side bursting up-back off the chest bone.
  bar torso on chest from=0.75 to=1.35 r=0.030 r2=0.005 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.060,0.070,-0.105) tip=(0.055,0.230,-0.160) both color=c9b896
  bar torso on chest from=0.45 to=0.95 r=0.022 r2=0.004 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.120,0.030,-0.120) tip=(0.090,0.130,-0.200) both color=c9b896

  # ============================================================
  # HEAD — sunk into the yoke, in the goblin/gargoyle idiom: BLENDED ORBS
  # plus shaped prims (owner 2026-09-07: not an oval, not a blockhead). The
  # skull bone runs (0,1.702,0.172) -> (0,1.841,0.228); offsets are world
  # axes off the anchored point. PROPORTION LESSON (paid for twice): a round
  # cranium (r 0.125, tall 1.15) swallowed every face prim — the eyes cleared
  # the muzzle front by 2 mm and the whole face read as a blank dome from
  # ahead. The plate's head is a LOW FLAT WEDGE: cranium slab wide> tall, and
  # the brow/eyes/muzzle stacked down its FRONT-BOTTOM slope, the muzzle the
  # most-forward prim. The jaw mass dips below the clavicle tops (~1.607):
  # the sunken read. NO big ears (gargoyle owns them), no geometric teeth
  # (walrus-goatee failure — the decal owns teeth).
  # ============================================================
  # Cranium: the low wide slab — semi 0.213/0.098/0.115, top ~1.90 where the
  # crown thorns root. deep 1.00: the decal's hs frame normalises by THIS prim
  # (fattest UNPAINTED head prim, radius*maxScale — lab-main's headShape; the
  # painted cheek is skipped), and the FRONT LIP must not overhang the face —
  # at deep 1.25 the lip reached z 0.371 and hid the brow/muzzle from every
  # front camera below head height (paid for across four close-ups).
  blob head on skull at=0.85 r=0.115 wide=1.85 tall=0.85 deep=1.00 blend=0.006 offset=(0,-0.020,0)
  # Cheek/jaw mass: the WIDEST-scaled head prim, and UNPAINTED on purpose —
  # lab-main's headShape (fattest UNPAINTED head prim, radius*maxScale) picks
  # it as the decal's hs frame. That is load-bearing: the maw sits at the
  # cheek's own height, so |hs| at the muzzle front stays ~1.5, inside the
  # decal's facing fade — against the cranium's frame it was 2.1 and the decal
  # faded to nothing (four close-ups paid for this). Its lower step against
  # the cranium still reads as the maw's shadow.
  blob head on skull at=0.40 r=0.115 wide=1.90 tall=1.00 deep=1.20 blend=0.005 offset=(0,-0.130,0.060)
  # Muzzle: the wide short barrel, the MOST FORWARD prim on the body (front
  # z ~0.48) — no pointy snout (the gargoyle owns the hook); this mouth is
  # all width. It must clear the cranium's front lip (z ~0.35) by a wide
  # margin or the brim occludes the whole maw from the game's eye height.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 r=0.075 wide=1.70 tall=0.70 deep=1.10 blend=0.005 offset=(0,-0.100,0.210)
  # Maw slot: a dark-painted thin crescent along the muzzle's lower front —
  # Brow ridges: PAIRED, tapered, angled outer-UP (the gargoyle's angry
  # slant — a first pass drooped and read sad). Seated ON the cranium slab's
  # front slope (q ~0.6 — half-embedded, the gargoyle's eyes sat at q 1.13),
  # NOT floating: an earlier monobrow ledge hung 88 mm clear of the slab
  # with nothing beneath, and the owner read it as floating, rightly.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 r=0.030 r2=0.020 blend=0.003 offset=(0.055,0.039,0.146) tip=(0.040,0.045,0.030) both color=c9b896
  # Ember eyes: tapered wedges on the slab's slope just under the ridges,
  # half-embedded (q ~1.05) so only the ember pokes out — a deep-set glow,
  # not a floating ball. High-set like the plate's eyes: low placements
  # drowned in the slab's shade. Each sits in a DARK-PAINTED socket ring —
  # on lit rust hide the bare ember washed out; the dark ring is the
  # contrast that makes it read as a sunken ember at gameplay distance.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 r=0.026 r2=0.009 blend=0.003 offset=(0.062,-0.004,0.118) tip=(0.018,0.020,0.010) both color=ff6a1a glow=0.9
  blob head on skull at=0.55 r=0.034 wide=1.30 tall=1.00 deep=0.45 blend=0.002 offset=(0.058,-0.002,0.104) both color=241408
  # Upper teeth: four small crooked points hanging from the muzzle's lower
  # front into the maw slot's dark band — inside the mouth line, NOT hanging
  # past the jaw (the gargoyle's walrus-goatee failure). Pale bone so they
  # read against the dark slot.
  bar head on skull from=0.40 to=0.44 r=0.009 r2=0.003 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.018,-0.132,0.266) tip=(0.006,-0.022,0.010) both color=c9b896
  bar head on skull from=0.40 to=0.44 r=0.009 r2=0.003 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.052,-0.132,0.266) tip=(0.006,-0.022,0.010) both color=c9b896
  # Crown thorns: a centre spike and a splayed pair, rising up-back (the
  # plate's head crest). Bases seated INSIDE the slab's top (an earlier
  # offset launched them from the air above it).
  bar head on skull from=0.90 to=1.25 r=0.022 r2=0.004 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0,0.062,-0.020) tip=(0,0.130,-0.100) color=c9b896
  bar head on skull from=0.95 to=1.20 r=0.015 r2=0.002 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.070,0.036,-0.045) tip=(0.115,0.090,-0.135) both color=c9b896
  # Maw slot: a dark-painted thin crescent along the muzzle's lower front —
  # reads as the open mouth shadow the plate shows. This REPLACED a hand-
  # authored maw decal after four close-up rounds: the decal pipeline itself
  # is fine (gargoyle's grin) but this head's hs frame is hostile to it —
  # against the cranium the muzzle sat at |hs| 2.1, inside the 1.95-2.55
  # facing fade, and against every frame prim the projection kept missing the
  # moving target of brim-occlusion + frame-prim choice + cache. A painted
  # slot has no projection to miss. Thin (tall 0.28) so it reads as a LINE.
  blob head on skull at=0.42 r=0.055 wide=1.75 tall=0.28 deep=0.55 blend=0.003 offset=(0,-0.155,0.265) color=1a0f08
  # Cheek thorns were REMOVED: every placement tried read as horizontal
  # handlebar rods crossing at the clavicle line (the head sits low enough
  # that its jaw level IS the shoulder line) — the crown + yoke burst carry
  # the thorn read without them.

# NO sheet block: the maw decal experiment was removed (see the maw slot in
# the head section), so the character falls back to the shared zombie-flat
# sheet like the dragon and the mouse. The face block below is shrunk to a
# nub — headRadius 0.001 kills the emitted skull ellipsoid pair,
# noseLength/browHeavy 0 gate the emitted nose and brow off — because the
# head is authored prims above (gargoyle precedent). If a later character
# copies this, raise the named `face skull off` word rather than copying the
# magic radius again.

# Face block: SHRUNK TO A NUB — the head is authored prims above (gargoyle
# precedent: headRadius 0.001 kills the emitted skull ellipsoid pair,
# noseLength/browHeavy 0 gate the emitted nose and brow off). If a later
# character copies this, raise the named `face skull off` word rather than
# copying the magic radius again.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006
  headRise   0
  headLead   0

# Rust bark: dark linear base (the shader sRGB-encodes, lifting low channels
# hard — authored numbers are darker than the rendered hide), olive-green
# mottle a HUE away so the blotches read as variation in the bark, not dirt
# on it (reference.md's palette rule). Dry-ish specular, no translucency.
# Wound interior stays the house red. Raising mottleAmp drags the mean toward
# the mottle, so the base sits a half-stop above the target rust.
palette
  baseColor     0.230 0.100 0.035
  deepColor     0.50 0.08 0.08
  charColor     0.09 0.08 0.08
  specIntensity 0.40
  specRoughness 0.42
  fresnelBoost  0.35
  translucency  0.05
  wetness       0.20
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.06
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.02
  mottleAmp     0.55
  mottleScale   3.0
  mottleColor   0.140 0.170 0.045
